# Files Git should never track. I keep this list short on purpose and only add
# an entry when something new shows up that shouldn't be committed. bin/ and obj/
# are created by `dotnet build`: obj/ holds intermediate files (like .o files in C,
# plus C# code generated from the XAML) and bin/ holds the final output (.exe, .dll,
# .pdb debug info). They are rebuilt on every build, so they don't belong in the repo,
# the same way you wouldn't commit target/ in Maven or node_modules/ in a web project.
bin/
obj/

# Editor settings folders (Visual Studio / VS Code)
.vs/
.vscode/
